/* book exam traps: Keep the minus sign: V₁ = AV₂ − BI₂. Writing +BI₂ with I₂ entering flips the signs of B and D, and the cascade product then comes out wrong. | A and C come from the open-output test, B and D from the short-output test. Mixing them gives B = V₁/(−I₂) measured with port 2 open, where I₂ = 0 and the ratio is infinite. | B is in ohms and C in siemens; A and D have no unit. In the T network, B = 6.5 Ω and C = 0.25 S. | AD − BC = 1 tests reciprocity, not symmetry. The T network has AD − BC = 1 but A = 1.5 ≠ D = 1.75, so it is reciprocal and not symmetric. | Matrix order in a cascade follows the signal path: [Ta][Tb] with a nearest the source. [Tb][Ta] for the T network gives [1.75 6.5; 0.25 1.5], which is the network turned round. */
